Nyx Linux tools

  nyx-updates     what is available to install. Installs nothing.
  nyx-rollback    filesystem snapshots, and a way back after a bad update.
  nyx-update-git  fetch and rebuild these tools from the GitHub repository.

About nyx-update-git

  It ships with the ISO rather than from this package, on purpose: if this
  package is the thing that is broken, the tool that fixes it still has to
  exist. Nothing overwrites it.

  It also only *builds*. Deciding whether to update is yours:

      sudo nyx-update-git
      sudo pacman -S nyx-tools

  What it does behind the scenes: clones or fast-forwards
  /usr/local/src/nyx-linux, writes VERSION as <release>.<commit count> so the
  package version always grows, builds with makepkg, and appends the result to
  the local repository at /var/cache/nyx-repo with a single signature database
  shared with the package that shipped in the ISO.

  After that the new version shows up in nyx-updates next to everything else
  waiting to be updated, and pacman -S nyx-tools installs it like any other
  package: it owns the files, so uninstalling removes them cleanly and the next
  -Syu sees the new version.

Useful options

  nyx-update-git --check    only report whether new commits exist
  nyx-update-git --diff     list the commits not yet built
  nyx-update-git --path     where the clone lives

Files

  /usr/local/sbin/nyx-updates
  /usr/local/sbin/nyx-rollback
  /usr/local/bin/nyx-apply-wallpaper
  /usr/lib/systemd/user/nyx-updates.service
  /usr/lib/systemd/user/nyx-updates.timer
  /etc/skel/.config/autostart/nyx-wallpaper.desktop

The timer is enabled for every desktop session already, via
/etc/systemd/user/timers.target.wants/nyx-updates.timer. If you ever disable
it, bring it back with:

  systemctl --user enable --now nyx-updates.timer
